# DianaSh golden corpus. Recorded from the C# shell, byte for byte; EMUSEN_DIANASH_GOLDEN=record rewrites it - see EmuSen_DianaSh.md §13.4.
# Patterns: <ROOT> is the sandbox's real root, <TEMP> the corpus's real temporary folder, <INSTALL> the install's real directory;
# a 'match' block is a regular expression the whole output must match, written where a line prints a time or a measured number.
command pkg
shell rust
usage 1   pkg make <path>...            a linked package for each game under each path (relative to the library)
usage 2   pkg ls [<console>]            the packages, with mode and state (ok, moved, missing, changed)
usage 3   pkg check [<package>...]      the game and every file hashed against the manifest (relative to Packages)
usage 4   pkg migrate <package>...      the game's saves, states and cheats copied into its package
usage 5   pkg wait [pkg<n>]             follow a pkg job that went on in the background

case the usage, and what a command line refuses
target none
covers 1-5
$ pkg
out 222
Usage: pkg make <path>... | pkg ls [<console>] | pkg check [<package>...] | pkg migrate <package>... | pkg wait [pkg<n>]
  Paths are relative to the library, / for all of it; packages are relative to Packages. See man pkg.
status 1
action none
$ pkg frobnicate
out 222
Usage: pkg make <path>... | pkg ls [<console>] | pkg check [<package>...] | pkg migrate <package>... | pkg wait [pkg<n>]
  Paths are relative to the library, / for all of it; packages are relative to Packages. See man pkg.
status 1
action none
$ pkg make
out 270
pkg make: name what to make, or / for all of it
Usage: pkg make <path>... | pkg ls [<console>] | pkg check [<package>...] | pkg migrate <package>... | pkg wait [pkg<n>]
  Paths are relative to the library, / for all of it; packages are relative to Packages. See man pkg.
status 1
action none
$ pkg migrate
out 276
pkg migrate: name what to migrate, or / for all of it
Usage: pkg make <path>... | pkg ls [<console>] | pkg check [<package>...] | pkg migrate <package>... | pkg wait [pkg<n>]
  Paths are relative to the library, / for all of it; packages are relative to Packages. See man pkg.
status 1
action none
$ pkg make nes --self-contained
out 119
pkg make: --self-contained is not in this build yet; packages are linked, and the game stays where it is in the library
status 1
action none
$ pkg make nes --zip
out 108
pkg make: --zip is not in this build yet; packages are linked, and the game stays where it is in the library
status 1
action none
$ pkg check NES --fast
out 264
pkg: --fast is not an option of pkg check
Usage: pkg make <path>... | pkg ls [<console>] | pkg check [<package>...] | pkg migrate <package>... | pkg wait [pkg<n>]
  Paths are relative to the library, / for all of it; packages are relative to Packages. See man pkg.
status 1
action none
$ pkg ls NES SNES
out 250
pkg ls: one console at most
Usage: pkg make <path>... | pkg ls [<console>] | pkg check [<package>...] | pkg migrate <package>... | pkg wait [pkg<n>]
  Paths are relative to the library, / for all of it; packages are relative to Packages. See man pkg.
status 1
action none
$ pkg patch add NES/a.nes a.ips
out 98
pkg patch: soft patches are not in this build yet; packages are made, listed, checked and migrated
status 1
action none
$ pkg wait
out 25
pkg wait: no such pkg job
status 1
action none
$ pkg wait pkg9
out 30
pkg wait: no such pkg job pkg9
status 1
action none
$ pkg wait chd1
out 30
pkg wait: no such pkg job chd1
status 1
action none
end

case with no library set, every request is refused before anything is read or written
target none
covers 1-4
$ pkg ls
out 87
pkg: AppSettings.RomDirectory is not set: there is no library for a package to link to.
status 1
action none
$ pkg check NES
out 87
pkg: AppSettings.RomDirectory is not set: there is no library for a package to link to.
status 1
action none
$ pkg make /
out 87
pkg: AppSettings.RomDirectory is not set: there is no library for a package to link to.
status 1
action none
$ pkg migrate NES/a.nes
out 87
pkg: AppSettings.RomDirectory is not set: there is no library for a package to link to.
status 1
action none
end
